      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let $O$ be the midpoint of diagonal AC.  Finding the length $OA$ and $OB$ is simpler than finding the length $AB$, so the length of the diagonal is actually the distance $OA$.  Let the common length of two sides of the prism be one unit to simplify finding $OA$ and $OB$, summing those sqaure roots and taking the square root gives\n\\begin{align*}\nOA &= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{10}{2}\\right)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{26}\\\\\nOB &= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{20}{2}\\right)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{211}\n\\end{align*}Summing those values gives $OA + OB = \\sqrt{26}+\\sqrt{211}$, so the length of the diagonal is the distance between two points in Cartesian coordinates where $x+y = \\sqrt{26}+\\sqrt{211}$.\n\n***Note to this vloggers tldr directly:\nsolve \nthe distance between two points based on the square root\\",
